This is a volunteer hours tracker for a nonprofit ("Down By The Border").

Tech stack:
- React 18 + Vite + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (auth + Postgres + RLS)
- @react-pdf/renderer for PDF generation
- React Router v6

Conventions:
- Use functional components and hooks only
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Keep Supabase calls in /src/lib/api/ as typed functions
- Use Tailwind for all styling, no separate CSS files
- Components live in /src/components, pages in /src/pages
- Use shadcn/ui-style component patterns (composable, accessible)
- Always handle loading and error states
- Never trust client input — RLS handles auth on the backend

Project structure:
/src
  /lib
    /api       - Supabase query functions
    supabase.ts - Supabase client
  /components  - Reusable UI
  /pages       - Route pages
  /types       - Shared TypeScript types
  /hooks       - Custom hooks (e.g. useAuth, useProfile)